 ## 🔥 Git Safety Protocol (CRITICAL) - Submodule Aware
 
+### 🆘 Emergency Recovery Protocol (NEW - After Merge Issues)
+
+```bash
+# BEFORE ATTEMPTING COMPLEX OPERATIONS - ALWAYS CREATE BACKUPS
+git checkout -b backup-current-state-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
+git add . && git commit -m "Emergency backup before complex operation"
+git push origin backup-current-state-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
+
+# IF OPERATIONS GET STUCK/FROZEN - GO BACK TO KNOWN WORKING STATE
+git stash push -m "Save broken state for analysis"
+git checkout docs/autoapi-namespace-fix-2025  # or known working commit
+git submodule update --init --recursive
+
+# FOR SUBMODULE WORK - WORK IN INDIVIDUAL DIRECTORIES ONLY
+cd packages/haive-agents
+git checkout -b your-feature-branch
+# Make changes, commit, push
+# NEVER attempt complex merges across multiple submodules simultaneously
+```
+
+### ⚠️ AVOID THESE OPERATIONS (Lessons Learned)
+
+```bash
+# ❌ NEVER: Complex selective merges across submodules
+git merge --no-ff --no-commit -X ours feature/other-branch
+
+# ❌ NEVER: Partial checkouts during active merges  
+git checkout other-branch -- src/some/path/
+
+# ❌ NEVER: Force operations without backups
+git checkout --force
+
+# ✅ INSTEAD: Work incrementally with backups
+git checkout -b backup-before-changes
+git add . && git commit -m "Backup before attempting changes"
+# Then do small, reversible operations
+```
+
+### 🚨 When to ABANDON Operations (Critical Decision Points)
+
+```bash
+# ABANDON if you see these warning signs:
+# ❌ 1000+ modified files in git status
+# ❌ 500+ lint issues in trunk check
+# ❌ Git LFS failures blocking pushes
+# ❌ Multiple submodules in conflicted states
+# ❌ Operations freezing/hanging repeatedly
+
+# RECOVERY ACTION: Go back to known working state
+git stash push -m "Save problematic state"
+git checkout docs/autoapi-namespace-fix-2025  # Known working commit
+git submodule update --init --recursive
+
+# Your work is SAFE if you:
+# ✅ Created backup branches first
+# ✅ Pushed individual submodule work to remote
+# ✅ Used stash to save uncommitted changes
+```
+
+### 🎯 Preferred Workflow for Cross-Package Changes
+
+```bash
+# STEP 1: Work in ONE submodule at a time
+cd packages/haive-agents
+git checkout -b fix/my-specific-issue
+# Make focused changes, test, commit, push
+
+# STEP 2: Cherry-pick to other submodules if needed
+cd ../haive-core
+git checkout -b fix/related-core-changes
+# Make related changes, test independently
+
+# STEP 3: Update root repo references individually
+cd ../../
+git add packages/haive-agents
+git commit -m "update: haive-agents ref for specific fix"
+git add packages/haive-core  
+git commit -m "update: haive-core ref for related changes"
+
+# AVOID: Trying to merge/coordinate multiple submodules simultaneously
+```
+
